# Free notes: they stay with the sentence above, or with the file if they come before every sentence.
Note: written by hand from the old intent.map; notes do not enter the formal IR.
The module "executor" overwrites the json document ".minimake/cache.json".
Note: before rebuilding a target it deletes its cache entry and rewrites it only after success.
The module "cli" uses the module "graph" and the module "executor".
Note: the order of the imports does not matter.
Note: two notes in a row stay with the same sentence.
If the value "code" is not 0, the module "commands" raises the error "MinimakeError".
Note: a command with a nonzero code becomes a target error.
# a comment between the sentence and the note does not detach the note
The module "cache" writes the file ".minimake/cache.json.tmp".
# atomic write
Note: writes tmp and os.replace.
# a note on a sentence with an error is dropped along with it
The module "x" frobs the module "y".
Note: this note disappears.
